xpert), Tab Bar (+Tab Item Active/Inactive nested), Program Tile (best-for-you), Challenge Card, Program Row (warmup), Round Row, Day Chip (active/inactive), Stat tiles? (Calories tile, Metric tile generic?) — keep tiles as frames built inline but a couple as components where reused: Heart/Steps/Sleep/Water tiles differ; make \"Analytics Tile\" too abstract. I'll create components for: Workout Card, Plan Row, Level Tag (3), Tab Bar, Tab Item (2), Program Tile, Challenge Card, Program Row, Round Row, Day Chip (2), Section Header? (simple text+optional link — inline fine, but \"headers... as reusable components\" per brief #4: \"Design all other states, the headers, the navigation and every business component as reusable components\". So headers should be components too: \"Screen Header\" (title only) and \"Nav Header\" (back + title). OK create those.\n\nThat's a lot of components; manageable via script.\n\nSimplification decision: I'll create components with absolute positioning inside (no auto-layout) to keep code predictable. Hmm, auto-layout would be more robust for text widths (hug). But plugin auto-layout code is verbose. Text nodes: I'll set textAutoResize WIDTH_AND_HEIGHT for labels (auto width) and FIXED for paragraphs. Absolute positioning with measured text — risk of overlap if my width estimates are off. Mitigation: use textAutoResize HEIGHT with fixed width for paragraphs; for labels use auto-size and read .width after set to position subsequent elements. I'll write code that measures and positions sequentially.\n\nEmoji: \"Good Morning 🔥\" and \"Keep it Up! 💪\" — emoji via fallback font; fine.\n\nLevel tag data: Intermediate for Push Up; Beginner for Sit Up, Knee Push Up; Explore: Beginner×2, Expert (Plank), Intermediate (Biceps); warmup: Beginner×2.\n\nPrototype reactions:\n- 01: Button instance → 02_Home (NAVIGATE).\n- 02: WorkoutCard 1 (Lower Body Training) → 04_Workout; TabBar Explore item → 03; Analytics item → 05. (Home item → 02 itself? optional;