 FILL scaleMode crop correctly. cornerRadius override on instance OK.\n\nIcon recolor helper:\n```js\nfunction recolor(node, hex) {\n  const paint = { type: 'SOLID', color: hexToRgb(hex) };\n  for (const c of node.findAll(n => 'strokes' in n || 'fills' in n)) {\n    if ('strokes' in c && c.strokes && c.strokes.length) c.strokes = [paint];\n    if ('fills' in c && c.fills && c.fills.length && c.fills !== figma.mixed && c.type !== 'TEXT' ? ... \n  }\n}\n```\nCareful: for status bar glyphs (Signal/Wifi/Battery frames with children) recolor fills to white; text \"9:41\" fill white. Notch stays black. For icons (stroke-based): set strokes on all vector descendants.\n\nImplementation structure — scripts:\n\nSCRIPT 1 (setup & clone): \n- setCurrentPage(7:2)\n- Load fonts: Lato Regular, Bold, Black, Inter Semi Bold (for potential status bar text edits — not needed since not editing; skip Inter).\n- Clone source components → workspace at organized coordinates:\n  - \"Components\" section x=600..: Button 1:28 at (600, 0); Button/Pressed + Disabled I create new; Text Field 1:31 at (600, 80); Status Bar 1:38 (600, 180); Home Indicator 1:49 (600, 240)...\n  Actually source components must be CLONED into workspace page (copy). Then my new components created on workspace page.\n  - Media section: photos grid x=1000.., y=0.. \n  Return JSON: {button: id, textField: id, statusBar: id, homeInd: id, photos: {name: id}, icons: {name: id}, map: id}\n\nNote: cloning component into another page — clone() puts it in same parent; then appendChild to workspace page. ComponentNode.clone() → new component in same page? Then page.appendChild moves it. Fine.\n\nIcon/photo names contain underscores (Photo_Lower_Body_Training) — keep.\n\nSCRIPT 2 (design system components): create my components on workspace page in a \"My Components\" region (e.g., x=600, y=400 downward; media at x=1000+). Components:\n- Level Tag / Beginner (pill: bg limeTint #E9F7C8? text #567D0D, 12 Bold, padding 10×4, radius 9