r different metric tiles (Heart, Steps, Sleep, Water) share layout: white card, icon chip, value, label, extra (chart/bar). Create component \"Metric Tile\" with overrides? Charts differ (heart line chart, steps progress bar, sleep bars, water dots) — can't override shapes per instance. Compromise: create components for the four metric tiles individually? They're used once each — component-izing adds no reuse value; brief's evaluation: \"Component reuse\" — I have plenty. I'll component-ize: Workout Card, Plan Row, Level Tag, Tab Bar + items, Program Tile, Program Row, Challenge Card, Round Row, Day Chip, Icon Buttons, Section Header, Screen Header, Nav Header, Stat Chip (the Time/Burn chips on 04, reused twice ✓), Calendar Card? (once), tiles built inline. Good enough.\n\n- Stat Chip (171×52): white radius 12: icon 16 lime-bg? design: icon in 28 lime-tint circle? Simple: icon instance (timer/fire) 18 charcoal? Recolor lime? Icon_Fire with lime stroke on white — meh contrast; use charcoal icons with lime tint circle bg 28. Label \"Time\" 11 secondary x46 y10; value \"50 min\" 15 Bold x46 y26. \n\nOK. This is a LOT. Let me be pragmatic about code size: each use_figma call ≤ 50000 chars. I'll split into ~6 scripts. Use helper functions repeated per script (define in each script).\n\nCommon helpers per script:\n```js\nconst P = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('7:2'); // page\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(P);\nconst F = (r,g,b)=>[{type:'SOLID',color:{r:r/255,g:g/255,b:b/255}}];\nconst C = { lime:{r:0.7333,g:0.9490,b:0.2745}, charcoal:{r:0.098,g:0.1294,b:0.149}, ... }\nasync function txt(chars, size, style, colorHex, opts) { const t = figma.createText(); t.fontName = {family:'Lato', style}; t.fontSize=size; t.characters=chars; t.fills=F(...); ... }\n```\nWait: createText defaults font Inter Regular; must load Lato before setting fontName. Load all: Regular, Bold, Black. Also load Inter Regular? If any text uses default Inter (status bar \"9:41\" already exists in cloned comps — no edits needed). Only load Lato styles + maybe Inter Semi Bold not needed.\n\nhexToRgb helper.\n\nInstance helper: const comp = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id); const inst = comp.createInstance();\n\nFor icons: inst = iconComp.createInstance(); resize? Icons 24×24 — resize to 14/16/20 via inst.resize(w,h) — stroke weights scale? No, strokes don't scale on resize (strokeWeight fixed) — line icons resized to 14 will have relatively thicker strokes (1.49 weight on 14px icon = chunky). Acceptable-ish; or keep icons ≥ 16. Use 16 min for small icons, strokeWeight override to ~1.2 on shrink. I can set strokeWeight on vectors inside instance. I'll add helper recolorIcon(inst, hex, weight?) that recolors strokes (and fills if any non-hidden? icons have hidden fill white — leave).\n\nTab icons 20–24. Meta icons 14–16 (weight 1.3).\n\nAlso need photo instance helper: photoInst(name, w, h, radius) → createInstance, resize, set cornerRadius (all or per-corner), maybe.\n\nShadow helper: node.effects = [{type:'DROP_SHADOW', color:{r,g,b,a}, offset:{x:0,y:6}, radius:16, spread:0, visible:true, blendMode:'NORMAL'}].\n\nGradient: {type:'GRADIENT_LINEAR', gradientTransform:[[0,1,0],[-1,0,1]] (top→bottom), gradientStops:[{position:0,color:{r,g,b,a}},...]}.\n\nLayout: absolute positioning in screen frames; frames clipsContent = true.\n\nFlow: after building 5 frames (positions: 01 at x=0, 02 x=470, 03 x=940, 04 x=1410, 05 x=1880; y=0), set reactions + hotspots, then screenshots.\n\nNames: frames EXACTLY \"01_Onboarding\", \"02_Home\", \"03_Explore\", \"04_Workout\", \"05_Analytics\".\n\nLet me also copy default components with proper names (clone keeps name).\n\nOne more thing: figma.createRectangle etc. fine. Rounded rect per-corner: node.topLeftRadius etc.\n\nAuto-layout: I'll avoid entirely; absolute positions with measured text widths (t.resize? for auto-size: t.textAutoResize = 'WIDTH_AND_HEIGHT' then read t.width).\n\nFor centered text in fixed boxes: create text with autoResize then center manually: t.x = boxX + (boxW - t.width)/2.\n\nPlan scripts:\nS1: clone all source comps into workspace + create my base components (tags, tab items, tab bar, headers, icon buttons, stat chip). Return id map.\nS2: build 01_Onboarding + 02_Home (using id map via figma.getNodeByIdAsync — I'll hardcode returned IDs in next scripts, or store map on page.setPluginData? setPluginData is... wait \"MUST NEVER use loadAllPagesAsync, setPluginData, createImageAsync\" — setPluginData banned! So pass IDs via returned JSON → I read tool result → hardcode in next script. Fine.\nS3: build 03_Explore.\nS4: build 04_Workout.\nS5: build 05_Analytics.\nS6: reactions + flow starting points.\nScreenshots each (or after all).\n\nAlso: \"createImageAsync\" banned but figma.createImage? Not needed — using image fills via component clones/instances.\n\nEmoji in text: font Lato, characters with emoji — should work (Figma auto emoji fallback).\n\nLet me also double check component clone: 15 photos + map + 15 icons + 4 = 35 clones. Do in one script with a loop. Coordinates: media grid: photos 130×100 cells at x=1000..; icons at x=1000 y=600 cells 60×40; etc. Neat but not critical — organize simply:\n- Default components: x 600 col: Button (600,0), Text Field (600,80), Status Bar (600,180), Home Indicator (600,250).\n- Photos: grid 5 cols × 3 rows, cell 260×190, start (600, 320): Photo_Onboarding(240w)... just place sequentially with 20 gaps in rows by max width 285.\n- Map at end.\n- Icons: grid 8 cols × 2 rows cell 60×60 start (600, 1000)?? Wait my own components also need space. Layout workspace:\n  - Screens row: y=0, x = 0, 470, 940, 1410, 1880 (390 wide each + 80 gap).\n  - Components section: y = 1000: default comps at (0,1000) region; my comps (0,1200..); media library (0, 1700...). Let me organize:\n    - \"Copied components\" label + Button(0,1040), TextField(400,1040), StatusBar(800,1040), HomeInd(1250,1040)\n    - \"My components\" starting y1150: grid placements