con_Profile:'5:27', Icon_Search:'5:28', Icon_Sleep:'5:29', Icon_Steps:'5:30', Icon_Timer:'5:31', Icon_Water:'5:32' };\nout.icons = {};\nlet ix = 0, iy = py + 220;\nfor (const [name, id] of Object.entries(iconSrc)) {\n  const c = await cloneInto(id, ix, iy);\n  out.icons[name] = c.id;\n  ix += 80;\n  if (ix > 1200) { ix = 0; iy += 60; }\n}\nreturn JSON.stringify(out);\n```\n\nWait — clone() of a COMPONENT: the clone is a ComponentNode on same page as original; appendChild(page) moves it. OK. But NOTE: these cloned components become masters in my file; instances reference them. \n\nAlso labels under media in source (text \"Photo_X\") are separate nodes — I'm cloning just the symbol (image only). Good.\n\nThen S1b create my components... could be same script but long. Split: S1 = clones. S2 = my base components (tags, chips, tab, headers, buttons, cards). S3 = 01+02 screens. S4 = 03. S5 = 04+05. S6 = prototype.\n\nLet me also verify icon component children count — Icon_Fire has 2 vectors; recolor all descendants with strokes. Some icons may have fills too; recolor both strokes and (visible) fills for vectors only (not text). Status bar recolor white: descendants incl text — recolor fills of text + vector fills/strokes, skip Notch rect (keep black — actually notch should stay black, it's the phone notch).\n\nrecolor helper:\n```js\nfunction recolor(node, color) {\n  const p = [{type:'SOLID', color}];\n  const list = node.findAll ? node.findAll(n => n.type === 'VECTOR' || n.type === 'TEXT' || n.type === 'RECTANGLE' || n.type === 'ELLIPSE' || n.type==='FRAME' || n.type==='BOOLEAN_OPERATION') : [node];\n  ...\n}\n```\nfindAll on instance children — allowed (read). Setting fills on instance descendants — allowed.\n\nSimplify: \n```js\nfunction recolorAll(node, color, {skip=[]}={}) {\n  const paint = {type:'SOLID', color};\n  const nodes = 'findAll' in node ? node.findAll(()=>true).concat([node]) : [node];\n  for (const n of nodes) {\n    if (skip.includes(n.name)) continue;\n    if ('strokes' in n && n.strokes && n.strokes.length) { try { n.strokes = paint; } catch(e){} }\n    if ('fills' in n && Array.isArray(n.fills) && n.fills.length) {\n      const allHidden = n.fills.every(f=>!f.visible);\n      if (!allHidden) { try { n.fills = paint; } catch(e){} }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\nCareful with icon comp: comp fills hidden white → allHidden → skip fills; vectors have strokes → recolored. Status bar: time text fill black→white ✓; notch fill black → would become white ✗ (skip name 'Notch'); Signal/Wifi/Battery children fills → white ✓. Good with skip list.\n\nFor Tab Item labels color: text overrides per instance? In Tab Bar, all items inactive gray; on screens swap active item instance (master Active has charcoal). No per-instance text recolor needed. \n\nTab bar swap: in Tab Bar master, items are instances of TabItemInactive. On screen: tbInst.findOne(n => n.name === 'Home')... nested instance child name = \"Tab Item / Inactive\"? Instance children names mirror master internals. If I name each item instance in Tab Bar master as \"Home\", \"Explore\", etc. (instance nodes can be renamed), then tbInst.findOne(n=>n.name==='Home') → the nested instance → .swapComponent(activeComp). ✓\n\nMain screens' text overrides on instances: e.g. Workout Card instance: inst.findOne(n=>n.name==='Title').characters = 'Lower Body Training' — must load font of that text first (Lato Bold loaded ✓). Setting characters on instance text = override allowed.\n\nLevel tag: component per level (3 comps) — swap or direct create. In Plan Row master I place Level Tag/Beginner instance named 'Level'; per row instance swap to correct level comp. Same pattern as tabs. \n\nOK, also Program Tile tag: master has Beginner; per tile instance swap.\n\nNumber of use_figma scripts and size — let's go. I must be careful with ≤50000 chars per script; my scripts will be ~6-10k each. Fine.\n\nLet me now write S1 (clones). Also set page canvas? skip.\n\nOne concern: setCurrentPageAsync with page from another file position — page id 7:2 exists ✓.\n\nAlso after building everything, delete nothing; keep screens + components on workspace page.\n\nFlow starting points attempt (S6):\n```js\ntry {\n  for (const f of frames) f.flowStartingPoints = [{ flowId: f.id, name: f.name }];\n} catch(e) { out.flowErr = String(e); }\n```\nHmm flowId should probably be unique string; using frame.id as flowId may be fine (it's just an identifier). If error, catch & report.\n\nActually wait — I recall the correct usage: FlowStartingPoint { flowId: string; name: string } — flowId is a UUID generated by Figma. Setting arbitrary string may throw \"Invalid flowId\". If it throws, catch. Alternatively there's figma.createFlowStartingPoint()? Not sure exists. Try-catch it.\n\nLet me write S1 now. Actually, let me combine S1 clones + verify by returning widths. Go.","signature":"63f71fb5aae74bacb876458d"}],"id":"3d65be1d-56e3-4d03-b4f3-1a94a6d0b8e2","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0f6b2263-6330-4721-ac9b-b0791a58bf93","uuid":"fd130e3d-88b9-4a08-8fd7-cd402d855a9c","timestamp":"2026-11-02T07:20:13.327Z","thinking_duration_ms":466570}
