{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>mcp__figma__get_metadata, mcp__figma__use_figma, mcp__figma__whoami</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Complete a Figma product design benchmark in assigned file https://www.figma.com/design/tIT4HK1NS7E5MTNQAw4d7q/ (fileKey `tIT4HK1NS7E5MTNQAw4d7q`). The user's request (in Chinese): read the design task in「00·Start Here」, follow visual specs in「01·Foundations」, reuse components from「02·Components」, use assets from「04·Media」, and deliver the complete design to「03·Workspace」. Additional binding constraints from the system brief:\n   - Confirm account is zhengyaozhi@tetras.ai via whoami before writing (DONE, confirmed).\n   - Use only this assigned file; workspace page 7:2 is the delivery location; preserve all reference pages and their nodes.\n   - Build exactly 5 frames named exactly: 01_Onboarding, 02_Home, 03_Explore, 04_Workout, 05_Analytics (390×844, iPhone), wire as clickable prototype with listed links.\n   - Copy/data must match \"Fixed data\" verbatim; brand colors #BBF246 + #192126 and Lato are fixed; all other colors/type scale/spacing/radii/elevation are mine to define consistently.\n   - Build headers, tab bar, navigation and every business component as reusable components in the workspace.\n   - Use photos, map, icons from 04 · Media as instances; recolor icons as needed.\n   - Inspect screenshots of all required screens; fix visible problems; finish states + prototype flows.\n   - Response format requirement: prefix every tool-call message with exactly \"Reasoning summary:\" and end with \"Final answer:\" including assigned file URL, 03 · Workspace page ID, screen IDs, prototype work completed, and remaining limitations.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Figma Plugin API via mcp__figma__use_figma (JS code ≤50000 chars per call), get_metadata (XML structure), get_screenshot for verification\n   - Banned APIs: loadAllPagesAsync, setPluginData, createImageAsync. Must use `await figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page)` to change pages\n   - Font loading before text work: `await figma.loadFontAsync({family:'Lato', style:'Regular'|'Bold'|'Black'})`\n   - Prototype reactions: `node.reactions = [{ trigger: {type:'CLICK'}, action: {type:'NODE', destinationId:'<frameId>', navigation:'NAVIGATE'} }]`; try-catch flow starting points via `frame.flowStartingPoints = [{flowId, name}]`; fallback = transparent hotspot rects for nested-instance targets\n   - Instance overrides: fills, cornerRadius, resize, visible=false on children, text characters (after font load); NO repositioning children inside instances\n   - Nested instance swap for states: `nestedInst.swapComponent(componentNode)` (Tab Item Active/Inactive, Level Tags)\n   - Icons are stroke-based vectors (#1A1A1F, strokeWeight ~1.49): recolor by setting `strokes` on descendant vectors; helper with skip-list (skip 'Notch' in status bar)\n   - Photos/map are components with IMAGE fill scaleMode FILL — instances can be resized + cornerRadius overridden (per-corner: topLeftRadius etc.)\n   - Absolute positioning (no auto-layout), textAutoResize WIDTH_AND_HEIGHT with measured widths; running-y layout with overflow checks\n   - Component strategy: clone source components/media into workspace as local masters; build instances; swap nested instances for per-screen states\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **Figma pages** (fileKey tIT4HK1NS7E5MTNQAw4d7q): 0:1 \"00 · Start Here 设计任务\", 1:2 \"01 · Foundations 视觉规范\", 1:3 \"02 · Components 组件库\", 1:4 \"04 · Media 素材库\", 7:2 \"03 · Workspace\" (empty at start — delivery target)\n   - **Brief content (verbatim requirements)**:\n     - 01_Onboarding: Goal \"Feel motivated and start.\" Must include: Actions \"Get Started\"; Copy \"Wherever you are, health is number one\" · \"There is no instant way to a healthy life\"; Media Photo_Onboarding. LINK: Get Started → 02_Home\n     - 02_Home: Goal \"Pick a popular workout or continue today's plan.\" Must include: Greeting \"Good Morning 🔥\" · \"Pramuditya Uzumaki\"; tab bar Home/Explore/Analytics/Profile (current Home); Popular Workouts: \"Popular Workouts\" · Lower Body Training · Hand Training each with photo, kcal (Icon_Fire), minutes (Icon_Timer), play (Icon_Play); Search \"Search\" (Icon_Search); Today Plan: \"Today Plan\" · Push Up · Sit Up · Knee Push Up each with photo, daily goal, progress, level. LINKS: Lower Body Training → 04_Workout, Explore tab → 03_Explore, Analytics tab → 05_Analytics\n     - 03_Explore: Goal \"Discover programs and challenges.\" Must include: Banner \"Best Quarantine Workout\" · \"See more\" (Icon_Chevron_Right, Photo_Quarantine_Workout); \"Best for you\" · 4 programs (photo, minutes, level); \"Challenge\" · Plank Challenge · Sprint Challenge · Squat Challenge; \"Fast Warmup\" · 2 programs (photo, minutes, level); tab bar current Explore. LINKS: Home tab → 02_Home, Analytics tab → 05_Analytics\n     - 04_Workout: Goal \"Understand a workout and start it.\" Must include: back (Icon_Back) · \"Let's Workout\"; Description (see DATA); Header \"Workout\"; Photo_Lower_Body_Training; \"Rounds\" · 1/3 · Jumping Jacks 00:30 · Squats 01:00 · Backward Lunge 00:30 each with photo and play; Stats \"Time\" 50 min (Icon_Timer) · \"Burn\" 500 kcal (Icon_Fire); Title \"Lower Body Training\". LINK: back → 02_Home. NO tab bar.\n     - 05_Analytics: Goal \"Review today's activity.\" Must include: Calendar \"July 2022\" · S 10 – S 17 · current T 12; tab bar current Analytics; \"Today Report\" · Active calories · Training time · Cycling (Map_Cycling_Route, Icon_Cycling) · Heart Rate (Icon_Heart_Rate) · Steps (Icon_Steps) · \"Keep it Up! 💪\" · Sleep (Icon_Sleep) · Water (Icon_Water). LINKS: Home tab → 02_Home, Explore tab → 03_Explore\n     - Fixed data (verbatim): User \"Pramuditya Uzumaki · greeting “Good Morning 🔥”\"; Popular: \"Lower Body Training · 500 Kcal · 50 Min\", \"Hand Training · 600 Kcal · 40 Min\"; Today Plan: \"Push Up · 100 push ups a day · 45% · Intermediate\", \"Sit Up · 20 sit ups a day · 75% · Beginner\", \"Knee Push Up · 20 knee push ups a day · 45% · Beginner\"; Best for you: \"Belly fat burner · 10 min · Beginner\", \"Lose Fat · 10 min · Beginner\", \"Plank · 5 min · Expert\", \"Build Wider Biceps · 30 min · Intermediate\"; Fast Warmup: \"Leg exercises · 10 min · Beginner\", \"Backward lunges · 5 min · Beginner\"; Workout 04 description: “The lower abdomen and hips are the most difficult areas of the body to reduce when we are on a diet. Even so, in this area, especially the legs as a whole, you can reduce weight even if you don’t use tools.”; Analytics: \"Days: S 10 · M 11 · T 12 (current) · W 13 · T 14 · F 15 · S 16 · S 17; Active calories 645 Cal · Training time 80% · Heart Rate 79 Bpm · Steps 999/2000 · Keep it Up! 💪 · Water 6/8 Cups · Sleep (chart, values illustrative)\"\n     - Entry-only (NO frame/link): Profile tab, search, Hand Training, plan rows, See more, programs, challenges, rounds, Let's Workout, calendar days, report tiles\n   - **Inspected component styles**: Button = charcoal #192126 (rgb 0.098/0.129/0.149) fill, radius 28, text \"Get Started\" Lato Bold 16 white; Text Field = label \"Search\" Lato Bold 14 #1A1A1F + Input frame 350×48 white fill, stroke #E6E6E6 (0.9), radius 12, placeholder Lato Regular 16 #8C9093; Status Bar = \"9:41\" Inter Semi Bold 15 black + black notch 156×30 + glyph frames; Home Indicator = rect 134×5 black radius 3; Icons = COMPONENT 24×24, hidden white fill, vectors with strokes #1A1A1F strokeWeight ~1.49; Photo components = IMAGE fill scaleMode FILL (e.g. imageHash \"1303318356825b2c1d3108b2b8bb53adc6a4c9b7\" for Lower Body Training, map \"2d88dba0c75b137d509f091e4496e9031b9da2a6\")\n   - **S1 clone script (EXECUTED successfully)** — cloned into page 7:2 at y≥1060 (screens will go at y=0, x = 0/470/940/1410/1880):\n     ```js\n     const page = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('7:2');\n     await figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page);\n     // cloneInto(id,x,y): getNodeByIdAsync → clone() → page.appendChild → set x,y\n     ```\n   - **Returned ID map (memorize — needed for all next scripts)**:\n     - Defaults: button **9:2**, textField **9:4**, statusBar **9:8**, homeInd **9:19**\n     - Photos: Photo_Onboarding **9:21**, Photo_Backward_Lunges **9:22**, Photo_Belly_Fat_Burner **9:23**, Photo_Build_Wider_Biceps **9:24**, Photo_Hand_Training **9:25**, Photo_Jumping_Jacks **9:26**, Photo_Knee_Push_Up **9:27**, Photo_Leg_Exercises **9:28**, Photo_Lose_Fat **9:29**, Photo_Lower_Body_Training **9:30**, Photo_Plank **9:31**, Photo_Push_Up **9:32**, Photo_Quarantine_Workout **9:33**, Photo_Sit_Up **9:34**, Photo_Squats **9:35**, Map_Cycling_Route **9:36**\n     - Icons: Icon_Analytics **9:37**, Icon_Back **9:41**, Icon_Chevron_Right **9:43**, Icon_Cycling **9:45**, Icon_Explore **9:51**, Icon_Fire **9:57**, Icon_Heart_Rate **9:60**, Icon_Home **9:64**, Icon_Play **9:66**, Icon_Profile **9:68**, Icon_Search **9:71**, Icon_Sleep **9:74**, Icon_Steps **9:76**, Icon_Timer **9:83**, Icon_Water **9:87**\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No tool errors so far. One process note: `get_design_context` tool referenced in instructions is not actually exposed; only get_metadata/get_screenshot/use_figma/whoami exist — worked around by using read-only use_figma inspection script to fetch fills/fonts/structure, as the brief allows (\"read-only use_figma to inspect the reference pages\").\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Designed complete design system: Colors — lime #BBF246, charcoal #192126, bg #F6F7F5, surface #FFFFFF, textPrimary #192126, textSecondary #6C7671, textTertiary #9AA39D, limeTint ~#E9F7C8/#F0FAD9; Level tags: Beginner (limeTint bg, text #567D0D), Intermediate (#FFF1D9 bg, #A96E0A), Expert (#FFE4E4 bg, #D64545); Analytics tiles: Active Calories = dark charcoal tile with lime fire icon + white text, Training Time = lime tile with charcoal text, Heart Rate #FFE9E6/#F0503C, Steps green family, Sleep violet #E9E4FF/#7C5CE0, Water blue #DFF1FF/#2F9BDE\n   - Type scale (Lato): Black 30 (onboarding title), Bold 24 (screen headers), Bold 22 (home name), Bold 18 (section headers), Bold 16/15/13 (titles), Regular 14/13 body, 12 captions, Bold 12 tags, 11 micro\n   - Page padding 20 → content width 350 (matches default Button/Text Field widths); radii: cards 16, buttons 28, tags pill, input 12; shadow 0 6 20 rgba(25,33,38,0.06)\n   - Layout budgets solved per screen (vertical fits within 844): Home = status 47 + header + Text Field instance (hidden-label trick: place instance 25px higher so Input lands at target y, Icon_Search overlaid at input left) + 2 stacked Workout Cards 350×120 (photo left 96×96, title, fire kcal, timer min, lime play button 40) + 3 Plan Rows 350×76 (thumb 56×56, title, goal, progress bar + %, Level Tag fixed 100×24) + Tab Bar ~764–844; Explore = NO page title (fits budget), banner y56 h88, \"Best for you\" 2×2 grid of horizontal tiles 169×86 (photo left 64×86, title, minutes+timer, tag ~82×20), Challenge 3-across charcoal cards 110×84, Fast Warmup 2 rows ~46–48h, tab bar; Workout 04 = Nav Header + back (Icon Button instance for easy reaction), hero photo 350×200 r20, title, 2 Stat Chips 171×52, description ~5 lines Lato 13, \"Rounds\" + 1/3 lime badge, 3 Round Rows ~62h (photo ~46, title, duration, lime play 32–38), CTA button; Analytics = title \"Today Report\", calendar card ~120h (8 day chips 36×56, T12 active lime), 2×2 tile grid + full-width Cycling tile with Map_Cycling_Route + Sleep/Water tiles + \"Keep it Up! 💪\", tab bar\n   - State design plan: Tab Item /Active (lime pill 56×30 r15 with charcoal icon + charcoal bold label) and /Inactive (gray); Day Chip /Active + /Inactive; Button /Pressed + /Disabled components for state credit; Level Tag ×3 swapped per instance\n   - Component list to create (S2): Level Tag Beginner/Intermediate/Expert, Tab Item Active/Inactive, Tab Bar (390×~88 white, 4 nested Tab Item instances named Home/Explore/Analytics/Profile), Section Header, Screen Header (350×30 title 24 Bold), Nav Header (centered title 17 Bold), Icon Button/Back (40 white circle + Icon_Back), Icon Button/Play (lime circle + Icon_Play), Stat Chip (171×52: icon in limeTint circle, label 11, value 15 Bold), Workout Card, Plan Row, Program Tile (169×86), Program Row (350×46–48), Challenge Card (110×84 charcoal), Round Row (350×62), Day Chip Active/Inactive\n   - Prototype plan: direct `.reactions` on instance roots (Get Started button, Workout Card instance, back Icon Button, CTA not needed); for tab items use transparent hotspot rects over each tab area per screen (avoid nested-instance reaction risk); try-catch `flowStartingPoints`\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - “请在以下Figma文件中完成完整设计：Figma 文件：https://www.figma.com/design/tIT4HK1NS7E5MTNQAw4d7q/ 请先阅读「00·Start Here」中的设计任务，参考「01· Foundations」中的视觉规范，复用「02·Components」中的组件，使用「04·Media」中的素材，最终将完整设计交付至「03·Workspace」。” (Plus system-level brief constraints: confirm account zhengyaozhi@tetras.ai; use only assigned file; deliver to 03 · Workspace; preserve reference pages; final answer must include file URL, workspace page ID, screen IDs, prototype work, limitations; prefix 'Reasoning summary:' before every tool call.)\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - S2: Create my reusable design-system components on page 7:2 (Level Tags ×3, Tab Items ×2, Tab Bar, Section/Screen/Nav Headers, Icon Buttons Back/Play, Stat Chip, Workout Card, Plan Row, Program Tile, Program Row, Challenge Card, Round Row, Day Chips ×2, Button/Pressed, Button/Disabled)\n   - S3: Build frames 01_Onboarding + 02_Home (exact names, 390×844, at x=0 and x=470, y=0)\n   - S4: Build 03_Explore (x=940)\n   - S5: Build 04_Workout + 05_Analytics (x=1410, x=1880)\n   - S6: Wire prototype reactions (links listed in §3) + try flow starting points\n   - Screenshot 