{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"04_Workout: 15:372. All 5 frames now exist:\n- 01_Onboarding: 11:70\n- 02_Home: 11:90\n- 03_Explore: 12:176\n- 04_Workout: 15:372\n- 05_Analytics: 14:278\n\nNow S6: prototype links:\n- 01_Onboarding: Get Started button instance → 02_Home (11:90)\n- 02_Home: Card - Lower Body Training → 04_Workout (15:372); tab hotspots Explore → 03_Explore (12:176), Analytics → 05_Analytics (14:278)\n- 03_Explore: tab hotspots Home → 02_Home (11:90), Analytics → 05_Analytics\n- 04_Workout: Back Button → 02_Home\n- 05_Analytics: tab hotspots Home → 02_Home, Explore → 03_Explore\n\nTab hotspots: transparent rects added to frames over tab bar items. Tab bar at y756; items: instance children at x19+i×88, y=756+10=766, h56. Hotspot rect: x=19+i*88, y=766, w=88, h=56, fills=[], name 'Hotspot - Home' etc. Add reactions: node.reactions = [{trigger:{type:'CLICK'}, action:{type:'NODE', destinationId, navigation:'NAVIGATE'}}].\n\nReactions on instance roots: Get Started button instance (in 01), Card - Lower Body Training instance (in 02), Back Button instance (in 04).\n\nAlso try flow starting points: try-catch: frame.flowStartingPoints = [{flowId:'0:0', name:'App Flow'}]? flowId must be a valid Flow... Let me try flowStartingPoints with a generated flow — actually in the Plugin API, flowStartingPoints requires flowId of an existing flow in the file. Flows are created in UI. There's no API to create flows directly... I recall `figma.root` flows... Let me just try: maybe assigning a new flowId+name works. try { f.flowStartingPoints = [{flowId: '0:1', name: 'Main Flow'}] } catch(e) { note } — 0:1 is the Start Here page id, not a flow. Hmm. Actually I've seen that flows ARE pages' prototype flows and flowStartingPoints expects {flowId, name} where flowId is arbitrary? Let me just try and catch. Non-critical.\n\nAfter S6, take screenshots of all 5 frames and verify.","signature":"483f7d567d9b46a38debc26a"}],"id":"eaafeeaf-81b