{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>mcp__figma__get_metadata, mcp__figma__get_screenshot, mcp__figma__use_figma, mcp__figma__whoami</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Complete a Figma product design benchmark in the assigned file https://www.figma.com/design/tIT4HK1NS7E5MTNQAw4d7q/ (fileKey `tIT4HK1NS7E5MTNQAw4d7q`). Original user request (Chinese): read the design task in「00·Start Here」, follow visual specs in「01·Foundations」, reuse components from「02·Components」, use assets from「04·Media」, deliver the complete design to「03·Workspace」. Binding system constraints:\n   - Account confirmed zhengyaozhi@tetras.ai via whoami (done pre-compaction).\n   - Use only this assigned file; workspace page 7:2 is the delivery location; preserve all reference pages and their nodes.\n   - Build exactly 5 frames named exactly 01_Onboarding, 02_Home, 03_Explore, 04_Workout, 05_Analytics (390×844), wire clickable prototype with listed links; build headers, tab bar, navigation and every business component as reusable components; use photos/map/icons from 04·Media as instances (recolor icons as needed).\n   - Fixed copy/data verbatim (see §3); brand colors #BBF246 + #192126 and Lato fixed; other tokens my choice, applied consistently.\n   - Entry-only (NO links): Profile tab, search, Hand Training, plan rows, See more, programs, challenges, rounds, Let's Workout, calendar days, report tiles.\n   - Inspect screenshots of all screens; fix visible problems; finish states + prototype flows.\n   - STRICT response format: every assistant message containing a tool call must begin with a line exactly `Reasoning summary:` (concise decision summary in same message). Final response: first line `Reasoning summary: ...`, then `Final answer:` including assigned file URL, 03·Workspace page ID, screen IDs, prototype work completed, remaining limitations. Never issue a tool call or final answer without the required summary.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Figma Plugin API via mcp__figma__use_figma (JS ≤50000 chars/call); get_metadata; get_screenshot (use enableBase64Response:true + maxDimension:600 for inline image verification)\n   - CRITICAL BEHAVIOR: when a use_figma script throws, ALL changes in that script are ROLLED BACK (verified — a half-completed script left zero nodes behind)\n   - Banned APIs: loadAllPagesAsync, setPluginData, createImageAsync; page switching requires `await figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page)`\n   - Fonts: must `await figma.loadFontAsync({family:'Lato', style:'Regular'|'Bold'|'Black'})` at start of every script touching text\n   - WORKING reaction schema: `node.reactions = [{trigger:{type:'ON_CLICK'}, actions:[{type:'NODE', destinationId, navigation:'NAVIGATE', transition:{type:'SMART_ANIMATE', duration:0.3, easing:{type:'EASE_OUT'}}}]}]` — note `actions` (array), not `action`; trigger is 'ON_CLICK' not 'CLICK'; transition REQUIRED for NODE actions; no `enabled` key\n   - `frame.flowStartingPoints` does NOT exist in this API version (recorded as limitation, non-blocking)\n   - Instance overrides allowed: fills, visible, resize, per-corner radius, text characters (font loaded), nested `swapComponent()`; instance child resize (progress Fill width) works\n   - Auto-layout components: hiding a child (Text Field label) collapses instance height (instance became h48, Input moved to y0); auto-layout HUG pills rendered oversized when instanced → converted to FIXED size\n   - Icons are stroke-based vectors: recolor via findAll loop setting strokes (fallback fills); photos/map are components with IMAGE fill scaleMode FILL — instances resizable, per-corner radius overridable\n   - Drop shadow schema: {type:'DROP_SHADOW', color:{r,g,b,a}, offset:{x:0,y}, radius, spread:0, visible:true, blendMode:'NORMAL'} — all fields required (give helper default args)\n   - Tab per-screen state via swapComponent of nested Tab Bar children (Home/Explore/Analytics/Profile) to tabOn_*/tabOff_* masters; transparent hotspot rects (88×56, fills=[]) over tab areas for navigation reactions\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **Figma pages**: 0:1 \"00 · Start Here\", 1:2 \"01 · Foundations\", 1:3 \"02 · Components\", 1:4 \"04 · Media\" (all preserved untouched), 7:2 \"03 · Workspace\" (delivery target)\n   - **THE 5 SCREEN FRAMES (all 390×844, y=0)**: 01_Onboarding **11:70** (x0), 02_Home **11:90** (x470), 03_Explore **12:176** (x940), 04_Workout **15:372** (x1410), 05_Analytics **14:278** (x1880)\n   - **Cloned source masters in workspace**: button 9:2, textField 9:4, statusBar 9:8, homeInd 9:19; Photos: Photo_Onboarding 9:21, Photo_Backward_Lunges 9:22, Photo_Belly_Fat_Burner 9:23, Photo_Build_Wider_Biceps 9:24, Photo_Hand_Training 9:25, Photo_Jumping_Jacks 9:26, Photo_Knee_Push_Up 9:27, Photo_Leg_Exercises 9:28, Photo_Lose_Fat 9:29, Photo_Lower_Body_Training 9:30, Photo_Plank 9:31, Photo_Push_Up 9:32, Photo_Quarantine_Workout 9:33, Photo_Sit_Up 9:34, Photo_Squats 9:35, Map_Cycling_Route 9:36; Icons: Icon_Analytics 9:37, Icon_Back 9:41, Icon_Chevron_Right 9:43, Icon_Cycling 9:45, Icon_Explore 9:51, Icon_Fire 9:57, Icon_Heart_Rate 9:60, Icon_Home 9:64, Icon_Play 9:66, Icon_Profile 9:68, Icon_Search 9:71, Icon_Sleep 9:74, Icon_Steps 9:76, Icon_Timer 9:83, Icon_Water 9:87\n   - **My components (all on 7:2)**: tag_Beginner 10:2, tag_Intermediate 10:4, tag_Expert 10:6 (NOW FIXED 100×24); statChip 10:8, dayOff 10:16, dayOn 10:19, btnBack 10:22, btnPlay 10:25, section 10:28, pageTitle 10:30, navBar 10:32, metric 10:34, workoutCard 10:43, planRow 10:58, programTile 10:67, challenge 10:77, programRow 10:81, roundRow 10:91, tabOn_Home 10:98, tabOff_Home 10:103, tabOn_Explore 10:107, tabOff_Explore 10:116, tabOn_Analytics 10:124, tabOff_Analytics 10:131, tabOn_Profile 10:137, tabOff_Profile 10:143, tabBar 10:148, btnPressed 10:172, btnDisabled 10:174\n   - **Instance child names for overrides**: Workout Card: Photo/Title/FireIc/Kcal/TimerIc/Min/Play; Plan Row: Photo/Title/Goal/Track/Fill(width=pct×110)/Pct/Level; Program Tile: Photo/Title/TimerIc/Min/Level; Program Row: Photo/Title/TimerIc/Min/Level; Round Row: Photo/Title/Duration/Play; Metric Tile: Chip/Icon/Value/Unit/Label; Stat Chip: IconBg/Icon/Label/Value; Day Chip: Dow/Date; Tab Bar children: Home/Explore/Analytics/Profile; Nav Bar: Title; Section Header & Page Title: single TEXT child 'Title'; Challenge Card: PlayIc/Name; Text Field (9:4): 'Search' label + 'Input' frame, auto-layout (hiding label → instance h48)\n   - **Key helpers (reused in every script)**:\n     ```js\n     const S = hex => { const n = parseInt(hex.slice(1),16); return {type:'SOLID', color:{r:((n>>16)&255)/255, g:((n>>8)&255)/255, b:(n&255)/255}}; };\n     function recolorAll(node, hex) { const p=S(hex); for (const n of [node,...node.findAll(()=>true)]) { if ('strokes' in n && Array.isArray(n.strokes) && n.strokes.length) n.strokes=[p]; else if ('fills' in n && Array.isArray(n.fills) && n.fills.length && n.fills.some(f=>f.visible)) n.fills=[p]; } }\n     async function inst(compId, parent, x, y, name) { const c = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(compId); const i = c.createInstance(); i.x=x; i.y=y; if (name) i.name=name; parent.appendChild(i); return i; }\n     // photo/icon swap: const ph = r.findOne(n=>n.name==='Photo'); await ph.swapComponent(await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(photoId));\n     function sh(node, a=0.10, y=6, r=16) { node.effects=[{type:'DROP_SHADOW', color:{r:0.098,g:0.129,b:0.149,a:a}, offset:{x:0,y:y}, radius:r, spread:0, visible:true, blendMode:'NORMAL'}]; }\n     ```\n   - **Design tokens**: lime #BBF246, charcoal #192126, bg #F6F7F4, secondary #667069, tertiary #98A19B, limeTint #EEF9D4; tags Beginner #EAF6CF/#557A0E, Intermediate #FDEECD/#A16B08, Expert #FBE0E0/#C94F4F; heart #F0503C/#FDE7E3, steps #55A81